    "problem_statement": "When a TCAT commissioner's BLE link drops abruptly while a TLS session is still being torn down, the device should not immediately restart BLE advertising; it should remain not-advertising until the ongoing session teardown completes and only then resume advertising (reflecting any updated dataset). Additionally, the secure-connection state callback should report a consistent BLE-link/TLS-session pair exactly once per real change and never report a TLS session as established without a corresponding BLE link. Incorrect handling leaves the device advertising too early (before the session is closed) and can report an inconsistent or duplicated connection-state change.",
